{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '180,235p' attavo/verify.py; sed -n '810,925p' attavo/doctor.py; git show 88a93d33aaa09d2f56720f64238a13c401a7eb36:attest/specs/229/spec.md | sed -n '1,240p'; git diff --no-index --stat attest/specs/229/stub/attavo/build.py attavo/build.py || true; git diff --no-index attest/specs/229/stub/attavo/build.py attavo/build.py | head -200 || true\"","aggregated_output":"\n\ndef cmd_verify(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    item_id = argv[0] if argv else derive_item_id(root)\n    if not item_id:\n        print(\"attavo verify: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo verify: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    specs_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"specs\"]\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    item_records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n\n    latest_build = latest_record(item_records_dir, \"build\")\n    if latest_build is None:\n        print(f\"attavo verify: refused: no build record for item {item_id}\")\n        return 1\n    if latest_build.get(\"status\") != \"pass\":\n        print(f\"attavo verify: refused: latest build record is \"\n              f\"{latest_build.get('status')!r}, not pass\")\n        return 1\n    # A build is empty when its tree, restricted to the spec's own\n    # claims, is the approved tree there -- asked against the approval,\n    # not start_sha, so a build that adopted a prior attempt's valid\n    # commits is not empty just because this attempt owed no commit of\n    # its own (item 229). sha == start_sha (the shape a first attempt's\n    # own empty build always has, and the shape item 227's own build\n    # was) is kept as a fallback for a record with no approval_sha to\n    # ask at all.\n    build_sha, build_start_sha = latest_build.get(\"sha\"), latest_build.get(\"start_sha\")\n    build_approval_sha = latest_build.get(\"approval_sha\")\n    spec_dir = root / specs_rel / item_id\n    parsed, _ = parse_spec(spec_dir / \"spec.md\")\n    claims = parsed[\"claims\"] if parsed else []\n    empty = (build_is_empty(root, build_approval_sha, build_sha, claims)\n            if build_approval_sha else build_sha == build_start_sha)\n    if empty:\n        detail = (f\" (sha equals start_sha {str(build_sha)[:12]})\"\n                  if build_sha == build_start_sha else \"\")\n        print(f\"attavo verify: refused: the latest build record names no change{detail}; \"\n              \"nothing to review\")\n        return 1\n\n    forge_cfg = m.get(\"forge\") or {}\n    checks_command = forge_cfg.get(\"checks_command\")\n    if not checks_command:\n        print(\"attavo verify: refused: no [forge].checks_command in the manifest\")\n        return 1\n\n    build_sha = latest_build[\"sha\"]\n    build_record_path = latest_attempt_path(item_records_dir, \"build\")\n                reasons.append(disagreement)\n        elif exit_code == 2:\n            not_read.append(item)\n            reasons.append(f\"item {item} merged at {merge_sha[:12]}: not read -- \"\n                           f\"the store could not be read; {cmd!r} exited 2\")\n        else:\n            unsealed.append(item)\n            reasons.append(f\"item {item} merged at {merge_sha[:12]} has no statement in the store\")\n    if reasons:\n        return p.fail(\"; \".join(reasons), sealed=sealed, before_window=before_window,\n                      unsealed=unsealed, not_merged=not_merged, not_read=not_read)\n    window = f\" at {since[:12]}\" if before_window else \"\"\n    return p.hold(f\"{len(sealed)} sealed, {len(before_window)} before the window{window}, \"\n                 f\"{len(not_merged)} not merged\",\n                 sealed=sealed, before_window=before_window, unsealed=unsealed,\n                 not_merged=not_merged, not_read=not_read)\n\n\ndef proof_no_attested_item_is_empty(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any] | None) -> Proof:\n    \"\"\"Proof seven (item 227). Every merged, fully-staged item's passing\n    build names a change: its tree, restricted to the item's own spec\n    claims, differs from the approved tree there (item 229 -- asked\n    against the approval, not the build's own start_sha, so a build\n    that adopted a prior attempt's valid commits is not empty just\n    because that attempt owed no commit of its own; scoped to claims,\n    not \"everything outside paths.records\", so a commit that lands\n    between approval and a later attempt's start but touches no\n    claimed path never rescues or defeats the comparison on its own\n    account). Item 227 was specified, approved, built by one\n    invocation, judged by another, merged and sealed, and its build\n    committed nothing -- the executor left the stub in the working tree,\n    the gate read the tree, and main received the spec and none of the\n    change. Six proofs held over it.\n\n    [doctor].built_since: merges at or before this commit are before the\n    window -- named, never failed -- so the specimen stands on every\n    doctor run without failing the tenant forever. Absent, the window is\n    proof three's. A build record whose approval cannot be resolved\n    (no approval_sha at all, or one this repository cannot read) is\n    named as not readable, not failed.\"\"\"\n    p = Proof(\"no-attested-item-is-empty\", \"every attested item's build names a change\")\n    if m is None:\n        return p.fail(f\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no records directory is declared\")\n    records_rel = m.get(\"paths\", {}).get(\"records\", \"\")\n    specs_rel = m.get(\"paths\", {}).get(\"specs\", \"\")\n    records_dir = root / records_rel\n    if not records_dir.is_dir():\n        return p.fail(f\"no records directory under {records_dir}\")\n    items = load_records(records_dir)\n    complete = [item for item, stages in sorted(items.items()) if all(s in stages for s in STAGES)]\n    since = (m.get(\"doctor\") or {}).get(\"built_since\")\n    if not (isinstance(since, str) and since.strip()):\n        try:\n            since = proof_window_start(root, m)[1]\n        except WindowRefused as exc:\n            return p.fail(str(exc))\n    else:\n        try:\n            since = git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", f\"{since}^{{commit}}\").strip()\n        except RuntimeError:\n            return p.fail(f\"[doctor] built_since {since} does not resolve to a commit\")\n    merges, refusal = _merges_reachable(root)\n    if refusal:\n        return p.fail(refusal)\n    built: list[str] = []\n    before_window: list[str] = []\n    not_merged: list[str] = []\n    not_read: list[str] = []\n    empty: list[str] = []\n    for item in complete:\n        merge_sha, _ = merge_introducing_records(root, records_rel, item, STAGES, merges=merges)\n        if merge_sha is None:\n            not_merged.append(item)\n            continue\n        if _is_ancestor(root, merge_sha, since):\n            before_window.append(item)\n            continue\n        build = items[item][\"build\"]\n        sha, approval_sha = build.get(\"sha\"), build.get(\"approval_sha\")\n        if not sha or not approval_sha:\n            not_read.append(item)\n            continue\n        spec_md = root / specs_rel / item / \"spec.md\"\n        claims: list[str] = []\n        if spec_md.is_file():\n            parsed, _ = parse_spec(spec_md)\n            claims = parsed[\"claims\"] if parsed else []\n        is_empty = build_is_empty(root, approval_sha, sha, claims)\n        if is_empty is None:\n            not_read.append(item)\n        elif is_empty:\n            empty.append(f\"item {item} merged at {merge_sha[:12]}: build names no \"\n                         \"claimed change; nothing was built\")\n        else:\n            built.append(item)\n    if empty:\n        return p.fail(\"; \".join(empty), built=built, before_window=before_window,\n                      not_merged=not_merged, not_read=not_read)\n    window = f\" at {since[:12]}\" if before_window else \"\"\n    return p.hold(f\"{len(built)} built, {len(before_window)} before the window{window}, \"\n                  f\"{len(not_read)} without a readable approval, {len(not_merged)} not merged\",\n                  built=built, before_window=before_window, not_merged=not_merged,\n                  not_read=not_read)\n\n\ndef doctor(root: Path) -> list[Proof]:\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    return [proof_every_gate_rejects(root, m),\n            proof_one_item_every_stage(root, m),\n            proof_no_commit_lacks_record(root, m),\n            proof_no_stop_lacks_cause(root, m),\n            proof_no_invocation_lacks_record(root, m),\n            proof_every_attested_item_is_sealed(root, m),\n            proof_no_attested_item_is_empty(root, m)]\n\n\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-yDv3Cepa' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-7LDDi4gF' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n## Problem\n\nOn 2026-09-27 item #227 was specified, approved at a commit, built by one invocation, judged by another, merged through the queue and sealed in the attestation store, and its change does not exist. The executor copied the item's stub into the working tree, ran tests in the background, answered `done`, and never committed (83 events, 32 tool calls, none of them `git add` or `git commit`). The build's gate ran the criteria, the selected tests and the tenant's checks in that working tree and passed them; the build record committed itself with `--only`, `sha` equal to `start_sha`; the review read a build that changed nothing and passed it; `attest` on the merge group checked the chain and sealed it; six doctor proofs held over it. Main carries `attest/specs/227/` and `attest/records/227/` and not one line of the change.\n\nEvery statement in that attestation is true and the attestation is worthless, because two things were never asked. Whether the gate reads the commit: it read the executor's directory, where a file written and never committed is indistinguishable from one that is on the branch. Whether a build built anything: nothing in build, verify, the pass or the doctor compares `sha` to `start_sha`.\n\nThis item asks both.\n\nThe gate reads the commit. Each iteration's criteria, selected tests and tenant checks run in a detached worktree of `HEAD` (`gate_checkout`: `git worktree add --detach`, removed when the iteration's gate is done), never in the executor's directory. A file written and not committed cannot pass a criterion, a test or a check on the executor's behalf; a tenant checks command that writes beside itself writes into the worktree and is gone with it. The pre-executor probe (`[checks].probe`) still runs against the approved tree in place, as it did.\n\nAn empty iteration is told so. When an iteration ends with `HEAD` equal to `start_sha`, the gate runs (on the approved tree, where the criteria already fail), the log and the feedback both carry \"you committed nothing: no commit since <start>; N path(s) modified or untracked in the working tree, which the gate does not read\" and \"commit your work; the gate reads the commit, not the tree\", and the loop continues. An executor that answers `done` before committing on its first iteration and commits on its second passes as before (`test_an_empty_iteration_is_fed_back_and_a_later_commit_passes`).\n\nAn empty build is halted. A build is empty when the tree its record names is the approved tree outside `paths.records`: `git diff --quiet <approval sha> HEAD -- . ':!<records>'` finds nothing. The comparison is against the approval, not the attempt's own `start_sha`, so a retried attempt whose head already carries a prior attempt's valid commits adopts them and owes no commit of its own; an attempt that ends on the approved tree, whatever it left in the working directory, is what #227 was. When the last iteration ends empty, the record is `halted` with a new stop class `empty`, provenance `executor`, detail \"the executor committed nothing; ...\" with the count of paths left in the tree; an earlier empty iteration is fed back and the loop continues. The class is the executor's, so counsel reads it and a steer retries it under R3; no new family. `STOP_CLASSES` and the build and verify schemas carry `empty` (build/9, verify/8). The status can never be `pass` on the approved tree.\n\nVerify refuses an empty build. A passing build record whose tree is the approved tree outside `paths.records` is refused before any adapter runs: \"the latest build record names no change; nothing to review\". The build no longer writes such a record; the refusal is verify's own guard against any record shaped this way, whoever wrote it.\n\nThe doctor's seventh proof: no attested item is empty. For every merged, fully-staged item, the passing build's tree differs from the approved tree outside `paths.records`. `[doctor].built_since` names a commit at or before which merges are before the window: named on every run, never failed, so #227 stands on the record as the specimen and the tenant is not red forever. Absent, the window is proof three's. A build record whose approval cannot be resolved is counted as not readable, not failed. This repository declares `built_since = \"dae6d765f3d6\"`, #227's merge. The proof's test is dogfood like the other five and is deselected from `[tests].run` and the CI test job the same way; the doctor job runs it.\n\nNot in this item: re-doing #227's change (its own item, filed on this product once merged); a ruling record voiding an attestation (R4); reading records from `HEAD` in every stage (R5); an executor-side change to the adapter (the instruction already says commit and stop; a mechanism is what was missing, not a sentence).\n\nThe stub under `stub/` is the change: `gate_checkout` and the empty-iteration handling in `attavo/build.py`, the class in `attavo/stops.py` and the two schemas, verify's refusal, proof seven and the manifest key, the fixture adapter's `ATTAVO_FIXTURE_NO_COMMIT`, the self-tenant's window and deselect, and seven tests red on the tree (v0.29.0). `tests/test_cli_help.py::test_help_names_the_seventh_proof_and_the_empty_stop` is red on the stub by design; the help text is the build's. Four existing tests move with the gate: two in `tests/test_testtool.py` whose checks counter lived in the tree the gate no longer reads, `test_self_tenancy.py`'s assertion that the manifest has no `[doctor]` table, `test_own_records_guard.py`'s deselect count, and `test_stub_ratio.py`'s pinned `verify/7`. `python3 -m mypy` exits 0 on the stub.\n\nRetires: the working tree as what the build's gate reads; `pass` as a status a build with no commit can hold; a review of a build that changed nothing; a definition of done with no word about whether anything was built.\n\n## Claims\n\n- attavo/build.py\n- attavo/verify.py\n- attavo/stops.py\n- attavo/common.py\n- attavo/doctor.py\n- attavo/cli.py\n- schema/records/build.schema.json\n- schema/records/verify.schema.json\n- schema/manifest.schema.json\n- adapters/fixture/run\n- attavo.toml\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml\n- tests/test_build.py\n- tests/test_verify.py\n- tests/test_doctor.py\n- tests/test_cli_help.py\n- tests/test_testtool.py\n- tests/test_self_tenancy.py\n- tests/test_own_records_guard.py\n- tests/test_stub_ratio.py\n- tests/test_stops.py\n- tests/test_record_schemas.py\n- tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- an-executor-that-commits-nothing-does-not-pass.sh: on a fixture tenant whose executor writes the change into the tree and never commits, `attavo build 1` ends halted with stop class `empty`, provenance `executor`, `sha` equal to `start_sha`, every criterion non-zero, the log saying the executor committed nothing and that the gate reads the commit, and `attavo verify 1` refuses the halted build with no review record written\n- a-passing-build-record-that-names-no-change-is-refused-by-verify-and-the-doctor.sh: a passing build record edited so that `sha` equals `start_sha` is refused by verify by name with no review record; merged with its item's other records it fails the doctor's `no-attested-item-is-empty` proof naming the item and the merge; with `[doctor].built_since` at that merge the proof holds and names the item before the window; this repository's manifest declares `built_since` and the seven tests named exist\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-aZBz2Axq' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-Xxy9kHeR' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n {attest/specs/229/stub/attavo => attavo}/build.py | 73 +++++++++++++++++++----\n 1 file changed, 61 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-YtfIevuW' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-WfoaS0tC' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ndiff --git a/attest/specs/229/stub/attavo/build.py b/attavo/build.py\nindex 7f0e0e1..dc1090d 100644\n--- a/attest/specs/229/stub/attavo/build.py\n+++ b/attavo/build.py\n@@ -90,6 +90,36 @@ def matches_a_claim(path: str, claims: list[str]) -> bool:\n     return any(fnmatch.fnmatch(path, pattern) for pattern